.TH DATA_FILE_VERIFIER 1 "2026-10-06" "mu2e-pcie-utils 9.01.00" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
data_file_verifier \- check the DMA and data-block structure of DTC binary files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B data_file_verifier
.RB [ \-h | \-\-help ]
.IR file ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Runs
.B DTCLib::DTC_Data_Verifier::VerifyFile()
on each
.IR file
(a DTC binary file: 64-bit DMA size words followed by DMA payloads, as written
by
.B mu2eUtil \-\-binary\-file\-mode
or
.BR binary_dump_to_DTC_file ).
Findings are reported through TRACE/TLOG messages.
Does not open any device.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Usage, exit 0.
Any other option prints
.B "Unknown option"
and the usage, exit 0.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Always 0; the verification result is not reflected in the exit status.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.BR TRACE_NAME ,
.BR TRACE_LVLS ,
.B TRACE_FILE
control where messages go.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
data_file_verifier run1234_DTC0.bin
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR binary_dump_to_DTC_file (1),
.BR DTC_binary_file_compare (1),
.BR mu2eUtil (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Mu2e TDAQ group (Eric Flumerfelt, Ryan Rivera, Ron Rechenmacher and others).
Manual page written for the September 2026 DAQ mega-review from the source
at commit a5c0ce7.
